## Overview

- **Stack:** TypeScript, Next.js
- **Language:** typescript

## Commands

Run inside \`apps/web\`. Keep the \`rtk\` prefix.

| Task | Command |
|------|---------|
| install | \`rtk proxy pnpm install\` |
| dev | \`rtk proxy pnpm run dev\` |
| build | \`rtk err pnpm run build\` |
| test | \`rtk test pnpm run test\` |
| typecheck | \`rtk err pnpm exec tsc --noEmit\` |
| audit | \`rtk proxy pnpm audit\` |

From the repo root: \`rtk test pnpm exec turbo run test --filter=@acme/web\`

## Framework docs

Your training data may be outdated. Before using a framework API, read the version-matched source below and heed deprecation notices.

- \`node_modules/next/dist/docs/\` — guides bundled with the installed Next.js version (App Router in \`01-app/\`).
- https://nextjs.org/docs/llms.txt — markdown docs index; append \`.md\` to any docs URL for markdown.
- While \`next dev\` runs: MCP endpoint \`/_next/mcp\` (compilation issues, route compile) — prefer it over guessing from logs.

## Constraints

### MUST
- Keep \`strict\` TypeScript; fix type errors instead of silencing them.
- Use the ui-ux-pro-max skill for UI/UX design decisions (layout, colour, typography, components).

### NEVER
- Use \`any\`, \`@ts-ignore\` or non-null \`!\` assertions to hide type errors (use \`unknown\` + narrowing).

## Conventions

- Use the package manager already locked in the repo; never mix lockfiles.

## Rules

Read the matching rule before working in its area. \`always\` rules apply to every task.

| Rule | Applies | Summary |
|------|---------|---------|
| [javascript](../../.agents/rules/javascript.md) | \`**/*.js\`, \`**/*.mjs\`, \`**/*.cjs\`, \`**/*.jsx\`, \`**/*.ts\`, \`**/*.tsx\` | JavaScript/Node.js conventions — naming, modules, async, errors and logging |
| [typescript](../../.agents/rules/typescript.md) | \`**/*.ts\`, \`**/*.tsx\`, \`**/*.mts\`, \`**/*.cts\` | TypeScript conventions — strict typing, runtime validation at boundaries, type naming |
| [frontend-ui](../../.agents/rules/frontend-ui.md) | \`**/*.tsx\`, \`**/*.jsx\`, \`**/*.vue\`, \`**/*.css\`, \`**/*.scss\` | Frontend UI standards — component design, state, data fetching, accessibility, performance |
| [nextjs](../../.agents/rules/nextjs.md) | \`app/**\`, \`src/app/**\`, \`components/**\`, \`src/components/**\`, \`next.config.*\` | Next.js App Router — server vs client components, data fetching, route handlers, env vars |

## Skills

Skills live in \`.agents/skills/\` (mirrored to \`.claude/skills/\` for Claude Code). Load a skill when its description matches the task.

